# Paths here are relative to verify/, not to the repo root. They used to carry a `verify/`
# prefix, which matched nothing at all — every built binary and build log showed up as untracked.
*/verify_bin
*/verify_out.txt
*/verify_build.log
*/node_modules/
*/*/node_modules/

# Generated by the harnesses that need them: an RSA keypair (rsalegacy) and the scratch
# directories each python run works in. A private key does not belong in a repository, whatever
# it is for.
*/k.priv
*/k.pub
*/pyrun-*

# Other per-run outputs harnesses write beside themselves: compressed round-trip files, DH key
# material, sealed blocks, jest's scratch. All regenerated on every run.
*/node.br
*/ours.br
*/*.key
*/*.pub
*/node.bin
*/ours.bin
*/tmp/
